bodyText:
The director shall establish a program to assist dislocated workers to obtain employment through assistance, training, and related employment services which may include but not be limited to:

(1) Job search assistance;

(2) Job development;

(3) Training in job skills;

(4) Supportive services including commuting assistance, day care for dependents, and financial, career, and personal counseling;

(5) Pre-layoff assistance;

(6) Relocation assistance;

(7) Mediation services or other programs conducted in cooperation with employers or labor organizations to provide early intervention in the event of major business closures;

(8) Added costs to employers; and

(9) Stipends and allowances.
